[19:48:44] I redrew the closed fist as a Solo48 model. It passes `validate_icon()` (valid, no warnings) and `build_gate.py` (0 errors, 0 warnings), and it reads as a fist at native 48 px on both light and dark backgrounds.

**The drawing:** an upright fist seen from the front.
- **Outline:** one closed shape with straight sides, curving in at the base to a 20-unit-wide wrist.
- **Knuckles:** four rounded bumps with staggered heights, as in the generated image. The middle one is highest and reaches the top of the box (y 6), then ring 7, index about 8, pinky about 9.
- **Finger divisions:** three short lines drop from the gaps between knuckles, 9 units apart. The first two end on the thumb; the third ends free.
- **Thumb:** folded across the front with a rounded tip, and a short lower edge that ends free.
- **Curled fingers:** one curve runs from the thumb tip to the right side.

**Keyshape:** I kept the suggested SQUARE and made the fist the full 36 units wide. Four fingers need their division lines at least 9 apart, and the narrower shapes (VRECT_M, VRECT_L) only allow 7 or 8. The fist is therefore a bit squarer than the traced image (width/height 0.73).

**Metric issues:**

| Issue | How it was handled |
|---|---|
| stroke-width (info) | Redrawn at stroke 4, with every gap sized for it. |
| keyshape-short-axis | Fist widened to fill the box on x. |
| 4 clearance errors (knuckles and divisions 2–7 apart) | Knuckles and divisions now meet at shared points instead of running beside each other. The free division ends 8.4 from the thumb tip. |
| narrow-join 33° | The curl now meets the right side at about 40°. |
| 3 small holes (2.5–3.3 wide) | Knuckle tops are open bumps, and every enclosed finger space is at least 8 across. |

All nine were fixed. The first version passed `validate_icon()` but failed the build gate, because the curl ran parallel to the right side of the base less than 8 apart. I tested heel and curl settings against the gate and used a passing one.

**Compromise:** the wrist is short (5 units), because the knuckles, thumb band and curl take most of the 36-unit height.

**Reference:** I found no local Lucide fist original, so I followed Lucide's general construction rules. It isn't a human figure, so the head-gap rule doesn't apply.

Nothing was registered under `icon_set/model/icons`, and `published/`, the build and the gallery were not touched. The files are in `new-pipeline-test/output_png/20260929-1932-closed-fist/`:
- `closed_fist_redraw.py`
- `closed-fist_redraw.svg`
- `closed-fist_redraw.png`
- `closed-fist_redraw-48.png`

